* 100 W COMMON-ANODE RGB LED DRIVER   |   12-16 V in   |   3 x 900 mA   |   Arduino true-PWM dimming
* Stage 1: peak-current-mode boost 12-16 V -> 44 V   |   Stage 2: 3 x high-side-LED buck, constant off-time CC
* --- INPUT PROTECTION / EMI ---
* F1 15 A fuse
* Q5 reverse-polarity block\nD6 12 V Vgs clamp
* TVS + bulk. Cin ripple ~0.9 A rms -> use low-ESR.
* U5 = 78L05 / MCP1703-5002\nfed from VIN (5 V housekeeping)
* U6 LM4040-2.5 shunt ref -> IREF = 0.340 V\nsets 900 mA on all three channels
* --- STAGE 1 : PEAK-CURRENT-MODE BOOST   12-16 V -> 44 V @ 2.1 A ---
* R7/C13 snubber:\ntames SWB ringing (EMI)
* leading-edge filter
* Cout carries ~3.7 A rms ripple - low-ESR electrolytics + ceramics, not one part.
* 44.0 V = 2.50 V x (1 + 100k/6.04k)
* Loop must cross well below the\nboost RHP zero (~18 kHz here).\nR4/C11/C12 -> ~1.5 kHz crossover.
* U1 = LM5155 (preferred) or UC3843 + sense scaling.\n200 kHz, peak current mode, slope comp Se~Sf.
* --- CHANNEL R (RED  Vf 22-26 V) : high-side-LED buck, constant off-time, 900 mA ---
* common anode of the\nRGB die -> RAIL
* leading-edge + noise filter\n(essential: without it the\ncomparator trips on every\nturn-on spike)
* off-time = 4.53k x 470 pF
* --- CHANNEL G (GREEN Vf 33-37 V) : high-side-LED buck, constant off-time, 900 mA ---
* leading-edge + noise filter\n(essential: without it the\ncomparator trips on every\nturn-on spike)
* off-time = 3.09k x 470 pF
* --- CHANNEL B (BLUE  Vf 33-37 V) : high-side-LED buck, constant off-time, 900 mA ---
* leading-edge + noise filter\n(essential: without it the\ncomparator trips on every\nturn-on spike)
* off-time = 3.09k x 470 pF
* U_R/U_G/U_B = comparator (MCP6561) + NAND latch (74HC132) + gate driver (UCC27517).  See LEDCOT.sub.
* --- ARDUINO PWM INPUTS : filtered + Schmitt-buffered (74HCT14) ---
* Rp/Cp = 1 us RC (kills switching pickup, passes 1 kHz PWM).\nRd 10k pull-down: a disconnected wire = LED OFF (fail-safe).\nDc clamps overshoot.  74HCT14 gives TTL thresholds + ~0.9 V\nhysteresis, so the Arduino ground can bounce and the driver\nstill sees clean edges.  Two inverters restore polarity.
.tran 0 3m 0 100n uic
.inc LEDCOT.sub
.inc BOOSTPCM.sub
.model LEDRED D(Is=1.86e-9 N=46.4 Rs=0.01 Cjo=2n)   ; 24 V @ 900 mA
.model LEDGRN D(Is=5.05e-12 N=52.2 Rs=0.01 Cjo=2n)  ; 35 V @ 900 mA
.model LEDBLU D(Is=5.05e-12 N=52.2 Rs=0.01 Cjo=2n)  ; 35 V @ 900 mA
.model MBR20100 D(Is=5e-7 N=1.15 Rs=0.012 Cjo=300p)
.model SS3H10   D(Is=5e-8 N=1.2  Rs=0.05  Cjo=50p)
.model BZX84C12 D(Is=1e-14 N=1 Rs=1 Vj=0.7 BV=12 Ibv=1m)
.model BZX84C5V1 D(Is=1e-14 N=1 Rs=1 Vj=0.7 BV=5.1 Ibv=1m)
.model SMDJ18A  D(Is=1e-14 N=1 Rs=0.1 Vj=0.7 BV=20 Ibv=1m)
.model IRFB4110  VDMOS(Rg=2 Vto=3.5 Kp=90 Rd=3.5m Rs=1m Cgdmax=2n Cgdmin=0.1n Cgs=6n Cjo=1.5n Is=8e-8 Rb=6m mfg=IR Vds=100 Ron=4.5m Qg=150n)
.model FQD13N10L VDMOS(Rg=3 Vto=1.8 Kp=18 Rd=115m Rs=5m Cgdmax=0.6n Cgdmin=0.02n Cgs=0.9n Cjo=0.25n Is=2e-8 Rb=30m mfg=ON Vds=100 Ron=135m Qg=15n)
.model IRF4905   VDMOS(pchan Rg=3 Vto=-4 Kp=25 Rd=18m Rs=2m Cgdmax=1n Cgdmin=0.05n Cgs=2n Cjo=1n Is=1e-8 Rb=20m mfg=IR Vds=-55 Ron=20m)
.options plotwinsize=0 reltol=2e-3 trtol=7
